@startuml
title Diagrama de Secuencia - Crear Aula (CLI HTTP)

actor "Administrador" as Admin
participant "CLI (Click)" as CLI
participant "APIClient" as Client
participant "API (FastAPI)" as API
participant "AulaService" as Service
participant "AulaRepository" as Repo
database "Base de Datos" as DB

Admin -> CLI: Ejecuta 'sighor aulas create'
activate CLI
CLI -> Admin: Prompt: Nombre del aula?
Admin -> CLI: Ingresa nombre
CLI -> Admin: Prompt: Capacidad?
Admin -> CLI: Ingresa capacidad
CLI -> Admin: Prompt: Edificio?
Admin -> CLI: Ingresa edificio
CLI -> Client: post('/aulas', data={'nombre', 'capacidad', 'edificio'})
activate Client
Client -> API: POST /aulas (AulaCreate JSON + Bearer Token)
activate API
API -> Service: crear_aula(aula_create)
activate Service
Service -> Repo: create(aula_model)
activate Repo
Repo -> DB: INSERT INTO aulas (nombre, capacidad, edificio)
activate DB
DB --> Repo: ID nueva aula
deactivate DB
Repo --> Service: Aula (con ID)
deactivate Repo
Service --> API: AulaResponse
deactivate Service
API --> Client: 201 Created (Aula JSON)
deactivate API
Client --> CLI: Response(201, aula_json)
deactivate Client
CLI --> Admin: Aula creada exitosamente (ID: {id})
deactivate CLI

note right of API
  **Backend FastAPI reutilizado:**
  - AulaService
  - AulaRepository
  - Validación Pydantic (AulaCreate)
  Sin modificaciones
end note

@enduml
